WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.819
The death of a great hero is just the start
of the tragic turns in "Black Panther: Wakanda

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:05.819
Forever."

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:09.540
If the movie left you crying, here's what
you might've missed in the explosive final

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.730
act.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:14.150
Shuri goes through many challenges as she
takes center stage in this sequel.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.310
First she mourns her brother, but after Namor
and his people, the Talokans, attack Wakanda

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.160
and cause the drowning death of Ramonda, the
Wakandan royal has even more to mourn.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.570
But let's take a step back before we get to
the third act.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:30.000
Early on in the movie, Shuri convinces the
Talokans who confront her, Okoye , and Riri

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.940
Williams on the bridge in Boston to take her
with them to their hidden ocean empire.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.090
While she's there, she bonds with Namor and
hears the story of how his people came to

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.489
live underwater.

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:42.520
Namor also gives her a gift: a piece of jewelry
that once belonged to his mother and is made

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.390
with the leaves of the plant that granted
the Talokans the ability to escape the colonists

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.829
in Mexico that were taking their land.

00:00:48.829 --> 00:00:51.579
"My mother told stories about a place like
this.

00:00:51.579 --> 00:00:54.200
A protected land with people that never have
to leave."

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.800
There are many parallels between Wakanda and
Talokan, one being that they're the only two

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.410
places on Earth that seem to have vibranium.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.260
When a plant plays a key role in giving the
Talokans the power to abandon the land for

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:09.220
the ocean, many viewers may suspect that there's
a high likelihood it may be similar to the

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.820
heart-shaped herb that Wakanda relied on to
create the Black Panther.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:13.970
This turns out to be true.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:18.220
While it takes Shuri a bit longer to put those
pieces together than it might take the audience,

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.850
she eventually discovers that she only has
to shift a few molecules around in order to

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:25.720
use the Talokans' plant to bring the heart-shaped
herb back to life.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.740
After Shuri successfully fabricates the heart-shaped
herb in her lab, it's time to test whether

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.070
or not it's the real deal.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:34.400
While there is no time to do the traditional
ritual associated with becoming the Black

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.100
Panther, Shuri successfully goes through the
fundamentals of the process in her lab with

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.250
the help of Riri and Nakia.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:43.900
It's debatable whether Shuri is the best option
for the Black Panther role, considering everything

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.440
else on the young royal's plate.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.580
But Nakia doesn't debate Shuri's choice to
take up the mantle or suggest anyone else

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:53.869
would be more suited for the role – at least,
not right away.

00:01:53.869 --> 00:01:57.539
Earlier in "Wakanda Forever," Shuri made it
clear that she does not believe in many elements

00:01:57.539 --> 00:02:01.680
of the spiritual or ritualistic beliefs that
many Wakandans ascribe to – including the

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.170
existence of the ancestral plane.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.539
Despite her insistence that she only believes
in science, there is still a small part of

00:02:07.539 --> 00:02:10.220
her that hopes to see her family again in
that mystical realm.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:14.030
But when Shuri takes the heart-shaped herb
and wakes up there, it's Killmonger who turns

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:15.110
up to greet her.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.860
Shuri is just as shocked as the audience is
to see him.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:21.640
While Shuri may be unhappy to hear it, Killmonger
suggests to her that out of all the members

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.269
of Wakanda's royal family, she is the one
who's the most like him.

00:02:25.269 --> 00:02:27.980
"I want the throne."

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.530
Killmonger's observations imply that Shuri
is becoming obsessed with vengeance, just

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.330
like Killmonger was when he was alive.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:37.040
But at the time they have their talk, Shuri
doesn't see that to be true.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.310
Ironically, her next move after denying she's
driven by vengeance is to go to M'Baku and

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.680
tell him all about her plan for vengeance.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.780
M'Baku initially seems hesitant to go along
with it, but eventually, he and Shuri agree

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.989
to join forces and take on the Talokans.

00:02:49.989 --> 00:02:54.370
Namor and the Talokans initially revealed
themselves because the whole world is looking

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.860
for vibranium in the ocean, and they're getting
close to finding it in the Talokans' hidden

00:02:58.860 --> 00:02:59.860
city.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:03.340
The Talokans had successfully kept their home
hidden for hundreds of years, and by any means

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.270
necessary, they'd like to keep it that way.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:10.000
They also harbor anger at T'Challa for revealing
Wakanda and its vibranium to the world, which

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.860
set off a global race to find more of the
substance.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:16.780
As the only location besides Wakanda with
vibranium, Talokan could become a target for

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:17.780
exploitation.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:22.000
With the stakes high for the Talokans, the
Wakandans are banking on a vibranium detection

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.530
device they installed in the Atlantic Ocean
getting their attention and baiting them out

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:26.530
for a fight.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:30.720
The Wakandans wait on the surface of the water,
wondering if the Talokans will emerge – and

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.390
they don't have to wonder for long.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:35.920
The Talokans soon erupt out of the water,
and when they find the Wakandans on the ship

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:40.330
poised to attack, it leads to a brutal battle
between the once-secret nations.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:44.290
As the Talokans and Wakandans fight on the
ship, Riri Williams patrols the air in her

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:49.080
Iron Man armor, working to lure Namor to Shuri
for a one-on-one confrontation.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:54.230
Riri and Shuri's gambit to capture Namor is
successful, and Shuri traps Namor under a

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:57.760
device she has set up in her ship that seems
to work pretty much like a really big hair

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:58.760
dryer.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:03.120
Namor has already demonstrated great power
as a fighter with land, air, and sea capabilities,

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:07.120
with mutations that enable him to be remarkably
adept at swimming, fighting, and flying.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.090
But his power seems to rely on the presence
of water, so the Wakandans reason that if

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:15.080
he's sufficiently dehydrated, he'll be significantly
weakened, which will make him much easier

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.080
to fight.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:19.620
On paper, dehydration sounds like an absurd
weakness for a superhero.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.440
When you think about it, it's kind of a weakness
for everybody.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:26.139
But despite how silly it may sound, the movie
treats this scene — and Namor's valiant

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:30.199
attempts to fight against Shuri's big dehydrator
— with the utmost seriousness.

00:04:30.199 --> 00:04:34.470
Namor is a determined fighter, so even though
he is weakened by the drying device, he's

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:37.110
still able to use his spear to escape the
machine.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:41.140
In an effort to maintain her fighting advantage,
Shuri commands her ship to fly to the desert,

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:42.840
slightly inland from the water.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:48.360
As they touch down, Shuri dons her Black Panther
suit, and she and Namor begin to fight.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.250
Meanwhile, in the ocean, the Wakandans are
preparing to retreat.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:55.710
However, as they do, a group of Talokans approaches
their ship riding two humpback whales.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:05:01.230
They throw a massive number of small bombs
at the ship, leading to panic and mass casualties.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:05.759
Despite the destruction, the Wakandans abandon
their retreat, and the fighting between the

00:05:05.759 --> 00:05:07.850
Wakandans and Talokans becomes more intense
than ever.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:11.830
While the Wakandans' losses are no doubt terrible,
there is still some redemption to be had in

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:12.830
this battle.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:16.850
Okoye takes on Attuma for the second time,
looking for redemption after he bested her

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:19.910
with ruthless precision during their earlier
fight in Boston.

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:24.020
Although her failure to save Shuri from being
taken by the Talokans in that confrontation

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:28.199
led to her dismissal from the Dora Milaje,
she comes back for her rematch wearing the

00:05:28.199 --> 00:05:30.820
Midnight Angel suit Shuri created for her.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:35.000
Whether it's the suit or simply her determination
to prove herself, Okoye manages to best Attuma

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.440
the second time around.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:40.660
Elsewhere, Riri is taking on Namora for the
second time after the Talokan warrior knocked

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:42.040
her out on the bridge in Boston.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:46.199
And just like Okoye, this time Riri is victorious.

00:05:46.199 --> 00:05:50.060
Back in the desert, Shuri appears to have
the upper hand against a weakened Namor – that

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:54.590
is, until Namor recovers his spear and stabs
Shuri in the abdomen, stopping her in her

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:55.590
tracks.

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:58.440
Namor is somewhat solemn about his victory,
informing her that things could have been

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.759
different between them and their two nations.

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:04.520
Clearly, Namor is still of the opinion that
Wakanda and Talokan should work together to

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:08.240
take on the whole world, mutually protecting
both their countries and their vibranium.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:12.030
"Are you an ally or an enemy?"

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:16.350
Unfortunately, Shuri is in no state to debate
Namor now, as she seems like she is very likely

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.310
to be dying from his attack.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:22.050
As she stands there struggling, she flashes
back to her encounter with Killmonger on the

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:25.820
ancestral plane where he asked her if she
would be noble like T'Challa, or take care

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:27.590
of business like him.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:30.780
This memory seems to give her the strength
she needs to jump back into action.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:35.199
Her checkmate move is a massive explosion
that injures Namor badly while she remains

00:06:35.199 --> 00:06:37.370
protected by her Black Panther suit.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:40.520
Shuri then stands over Namor, apparently poised
to kill him.

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:44.479
Yet, as she looks down on him with her weapon
ready to deliver a fatal blow, she starts

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:48.889
to remember everything that she's been through
over the past year, including T'Challa's death,

00:06:48.889 --> 00:06:52.330
the devastation of Wakanda by Talokan, and
her mother's death.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:55.430
Finally, she sees her mother, who urges her
toward peace.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:07:00.160
"Show them who you are."

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:03.719
Shuri stops her attack on Namor and tells
him that vengeance has consumed both of them

00:07:03.719 --> 00:07:05.940
– but it must not consume their people.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:10.500
Namor surrenders to her, and Shuri promises
to keep Talokan secret from the rest of the

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:11.500
world.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:15.000
Shuri and Namor fly to the site of the battle
between their peoples and stop the fighting,

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.389
declaring Wakanda and Talokan to have a truce.

00:07:17.389 --> 00:07:21.160
With the central conflict of the movie put
to rest, the characters start to return to

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.510
their normal lives.

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:26.150
In Wakanda, they replant the heart-shaped
herb that Shuri reconstructed.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:29.830
Shuri sends Riri home without the Ironheart
suit she created for her, but she does not

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:34.520
leave empty-handed; Shuri has also fixed the
car Riri was working on in Boston, which Riri

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.240
explains belonged to her father.

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:40.020
Then, there is a gathering of all of Wakanda
that fans of the first "Black Panther" movie

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:45.009
will recognize as the ritual T'Challa participated
in to officially become Wakanda's ruler.

00:07:45.009 --> 00:07:49.590
This time, the ceremony is meant for Shuri,
but when a ship flies in, and Shuri is introduced,

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:52.570
instead of the princess emerging, it's M'Baku
who appears.

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:56.060
As he jumps from the ship, he announces that
he wishes to challenge Shuri for the throne.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:08:00.759
In the ocean, Namora confronts Namor about
surrendering to Wakanda — a move she is

00:08:00.759 --> 00:08:04.750
none too pleased with — but Namor reassures
her that the surface world will once again

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:09.319
come for Wakanda and, when it does, Wakanda
will have no choice but to turn to them.

00:08:09.319 --> 00:08:13.039
Apparently, Namor still believes the world
is eventually going to attack Wakanda for

00:08:13.039 --> 00:08:16.780
its vibranium and he is prepared to bide his
time until that happens.

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:19.449
The truce may be shakier than it at first
appeared.

00:08:19.449 --> 00:08:24.590
Meanwhile, in America, Okoye rescues Agent
Ross from CIA custody, gleefully declaring

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:27.190
she has never seen a colonizer in chains before.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:31.350
Perhaps Okoye's actions were a bit of a thank
you after Ross was arrested for leaking secrets

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:33.110
to her and Shuri earlier in the film.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:37.229
One way or another, it seems the alliance
between Ross and Wakanda is set to grow even

00:08:37.229 --> 00:08:39.779
deeper than it already was.

00:08:39.779 --> 00:08:43.640
Instead of the ceremony in Wakanda that she
was expected to attend, Shuri is instead found

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.750
in Haiti where Nakia now lives.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:49.149
Right before the credits roll, Shuri goes
to the beach by herself and burns T'Challa's

00:08:49.149 --> 00:08:51.540
funeral robes in a fire on the beach.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:55.089
This is a ritual Ramonda tried to perform
with Shuri earlier in the movie, before they

00:08:55.089 --> 00:08:56.720
were interrupted by Namor.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:59.390
A mid-credits scene then picks back up on
the beach.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:03.730
As Shuri sits in the sand looking out toward
the water, Nakia approaches her with a child

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.190
at her side named Toussaint.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:09.880
Nakia introduces the child to his Aunt Shuri,
who realizes with surprise that she's meeting

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.180
T'Challa's son.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:15.660
Nakia explains that T'Challa and Ramonda knew
about Toussaint, but beyond them, the child

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:16.670
was a secret.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:20.690
When T'Challa learned he was dying, he prepared
his son and asked Nakia to keep him away from

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:21.770
the funeral.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:25.209
While these were clearly acts of love, it
is hard not to wonder if keeping Toussaint

00:09:25.209 --> 00:09:27.149
away from Wakanda was the right idea.

00:09:27.149 --> 00:09:31.160
On the other hand, the child seems fairly
content when he tells Shuri that Toussaint

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:35.399
is his Haitian name, but his real name is
T'Challa Jr. — a revelation that indicates

00:09:35.399 --> 00:09:39.670
that T'Challa and Nakia, despite moving him
so far away in secret, ultimately do want

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:42.640
to acknowledge that the child is the true
heir to Wakanda's throne.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:46.390
What that could mean for leadership in Wakanda
isn't clear, though, because, after Shuri

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:51.240
and T'Challa Jr.'s brief exchange, the credits
continue, and "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever"

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:53.880
comes to an end with a promise that Black
Panther will return.

